From 8984264dd1e4dc68778920525486eba9f28b6bfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:37:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] www: System Info names capabilities, Wireless Log as JSON,
 kit pages cleaned up (102.8 line)

- System Info shows the capabilities by name; tokens with no meaning on this firmware are hidden.
- Wireless Log refreshes every 10 s by default, not while its tab is hidden, and parses a JSON
  status (ajax_reaper_wlstatus.asp) instead of evaluating text.
- The Internet page checks the WAN MAC with rp.v.macUnicast (all-zero and group addresses
  refused).
- The kit pages' settings forms hold only the apply inputs; rp.changed creates the input of a
  field the form lacks. The posted fields of every page are unchanged.
- The menu draws only its own menus' glyphs; the firewall rail badge is gone from the model, the
  shell and the dashboard.
- Encrypted DNS uses the shared stylesheet (Wallguard too, in its own commit), keeping its own
  layout and its switch style.
- Analytics, Devices, Traffic, Mode Setup, Survey and Wireless send the page token with their CGI
  calls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
